# SMA Epigenomics Pipeline

> Genome-wide analysis of DNA methylation and transcriptional changes induced by combined ASO and valproic acid treatment in spinal muscular atrophy cell models.

---

## Biological Question

Nusinersen (ASO) is an approved therapy for Spinal Muscular Atrophy (SMA) that corrects alternative splicing of SMN2 to restore functional SMN protein production. Marasco et al. (2022) demonstrated that combining ASO with valproic acid (VPA), a histone deacetylase inhibitor, enhances therapeutic efficacy by counteracting ASO-induced repressive chromatin changes at the SMN2 locus.

However, VPA affects histone acetylation genome-wide in a non-specific manner. This project investigates the putative pleiotropic (off-target) effects of the combined ASO+VPA treatment by assessing:

- **Genome-wide DNA methylation profiles** — identifying differentially methylated regions (DMRs)
- **Genome-wide transcription profiles** — identifying differentially expressed genes (DEGs)

Comparing cell cultures treated with **ASO alone (ASO1)** vs **combined treatment (ASO1+VPA)**.

